title: "TEMer Plus: A Drawing Tool for Trajectory Equifinality Modeling (TEM)"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based drawing tool for diagrams of Trajectory Equifinality Modeling
  (TEM), used in the Trajectory Equifinality Approach (TEA) in cultural psychology
  and qualitative research. It handles TEM-specific elements (bifurcation points,
  obligatory passage points, equifinality points, social direction and social
  guidance, periods, and irreversible time) as structured data, and exports diagrams
  to PNG, SVG, PDF, and PPTX, as well as a Word report for papers that includes the
  notation declaration.
